00:00:03.610 --> 00:00:05.970
One of the topics that I'm
really passionate about

00:00:05.970 --> 00:00:07.180
is slide writing.

00:00:07.180 --> 00:00:09.483
And slide writing is
the science, or the art,

00:00:09.483 --> 00:00:11.794
of creating slide presentations

00:00:11.794 --> 00:00:15.680
in the style of leading
consulting firms like MBB

00:00:15.680 --> 00:00:17.880
and this is McKinsey, BCG, and Bain.

00:00:17.880 --> 00:00:19.180
As you probably already know

00:00:19.180 --> 00:00:21.270
if you're a regular
watcher of this channel,

00:00:21.270 --> 00:00:23.540
I worked at McKinsey for six years.

00:00:23.540 --> 00:00:25.670
I taught slide writing inside the firms

00:00:25.670 --> 00:00:28.410
to junior colleagues, but
I'm also giving trainings

00:00:28.410 --> 00:00:30.420
on slide writing to corporations

00:00:30.420 --> 00:00:33.000
and I also serve as a
lecturer on communication

00:00:33.000 --> 00:00:33.980
and slide writing.

00:00:33.980 --> 00:00:37.270
For instance, at the University
of St. Gallen MBA program.

00:00:37.270 --> 00:00:38.374
So today, I will help you

00:00:38.374 --> 00:00:41.000
to build your slide
writing skills as well,

00:00:41.000 --> 00:00:43.738
and I will do this by
reviewing slide presentations

00:00:43.738 --> 00:00:45.420
that you sent me.

00:00:45.420 --> 00:00:48.020
So I asked you on Instagram to
send me some of the documents

00:00:48.020 --> 00:00:48.900
that you are working on,

00:00:48.900 --> 00:00:50.376
for instance from university projects,

00:00:50.376 --> 00:00:52.730
and I received several
submissions from you.

00:00:52.730 --> 00:00:54.710
So we're going to look
into this in a moment.

00:00:54.710 --> 00:00:55.990
But before we do that,

00:00:55.990 --> 00:00:58.880
I just wanna be really clear on one thing.

00:00:58.880 --> 00:01:01.210
So maybe some of you are
asking yourselves now

00:01:01.210 --> 00:01:03.450
where did all my hair go?

00:01:03.450 --> 00:01:05.780
And due to the special
situation in Germany,

00:01:05.780 --> 00:01:09.150
all the hair dresses are
closed at the moment.

00:01:09.150 --> 00:01:13.500
So, no, I did not bribe any
professional to cut my hair.

00:01:13.500 --> 00:01:16.280
I just asked my sister to do it.

00:01:16.280 --> 00:01:17.810
And if you're following me on Instagram,

00:01:17.810 --> 00:01:19.350
you know exactly what happens

00:01:19.350 --> 00:01:23.220
and you also know why this
maybe was not the best idea.

00:01:23.220 --> 00:01:25.227
But let's not talk more
about this right now.

00:01:25.227 --> 00:01:27.370
Welcome to another coffee break

00:01:27.370 --> 00:01:29.280
here on my channel, Firm Learning.

00:01:29.280 --> 00:01:31.100
It's already pretty late here in Germany

00:01:31.100 --> 00:01:32.270
so I'm drinking tea.

00:01:32.270 --> 00:01:33.970
Please help yourself to a cup as well.

00:01:33.970 --> 00:01:37.840
But now without further
ado, let's jump in.

00:01:37.840 --> 00:01:39.560
So I'm looking now at
the screen in front of me

00:01:39.560 --> 00:01:42.370
where I open several of the
presentations that you sent me.

00:01:42.370 --> 00:01:45.230
So of course we won't go
over every presentation

00:01:45.230 --> 00:01:48.270
slide by slide, but I always
selected a couple of slides

00:01:48.270 --> 00:01:51.221
that I believe will be most
educational to discuss.

00:01:51.221 --> 00:01:53.050
So just bear in here with me and trust

00:01:53.050 --> 00:01:55.620
there are some very, very important

00:01:55.620 --> 00:01:57.660
and valuable slide writing lessons

00:01:57.660 --> 00:02:00.370
that we'll now jointly identify and find

00:02:00.370 --> 00:02:01.750
while looking at these pages.

00:02:01.750 --> 00:02:03.090
And here, let's start with this one,

00:02:03.090 --> 00:02:04.903
there seems to be some type
of university presentation

00:02:04.903 --> 00:02:09.660
about an economics class,
the Turkish growth miracle.

00:02:09.660 --> 00:02:11.770
So frankly, I have no
idea about the topic.

00:02:11.770 --> 00:02:14.180
So let's just look at this page.

00:02:14.180 --> 00:02:15.390
What do we see here?

00:02:15.390 --> 00:02:20.320
So my first impression is that
this page looks kind of messy

00:02:20.320 --> 00:02:22.900
but of course the question
is, why does it look messy?

00:02:22.900 --> 00:02:25.280
What makes this page look messy?

00:02:25.280 --> 00:02:27.206
And if you look into this,
probably the main reason

00:02:27.206 --> 00:02:32.024
is that this page uses all
kinds of different font sizes.

00:02:32.024 --> 00:02:34.830
And this is really a problem
that you see quite often.

00:02:34.830 --> 00:02:35.663
So let's look.

00:02:35.663 --> 00:02:37.850
Here of course, the action title 28.

00:02:37.850 --> 00:02:39.650
Here this title, 24.

00:02:39.650 --> 00:02:42.520
Red curve, depreciation 18,

00:02:42.520 --> 00:02:43.640
this one 20,

00:02:43.640 --> 00:02:44.473
this one 18,

00:02:44.473 --> 00:02:46.926
18 here in the chart 12,

00:02:46.926 --> 00:02:49.203
but here also in the chart 18.

00:02:49.203 --> 00:02:51.110
It's really all over the place.

00:02:51.110 --> 00:02:53.960
And I believe this
really significantly adds

00:02:53.960 --> 00:02:57.200
to this unclean, to this
weird unorganized look.

00:02:57.200 --> 00:02:59.290
So the key rule that
you always wanna follow

00:02:59.290 --> 00:03:01.090
when doing these types of presentations

00:03:01.090 --> 00:03:03.030
that the body of your slide,

00:03:03.030 --> 00:03:05.300
so everything except for the title

00:03:05.300 --> 00:03:08.580
and maybe some footnotes,
should be the same font size.

00:03:08.580 --> 00:03:09.920
So now let's look at the chart.

00:03:09.920 --> 00:03:12.260
Let's look at how this chart is created.

00:03:12.260 --> 00:03:14.200
And the first thing that pops into my eye

00:03:14.200 --> 00:03:16.720
are these very thick, dotted lines.

00:03:16.720 --> 00:03:18.820
So usually if you make dotted lines,

00:03:18.820 --> 00:03:20.930
you don't want them to be so dominant.

00:03:20.930 --> 00:03:23.440
You want them to be light
and in the background,

00:03:23.440 --> 00:03:25.790
but here because these are
one of the thickest lines

00:03:25.790 --> 00:03:27.800
in this shot, they're
very dominant, right?

00:03:27.800 --> 00:03:29.400
And this just doesn't look right.

00:03:29.400 --> 00:03:31.130
And next, this here, the different colors.

00:03:31.130 --> 00:03:34.240
So this is a green line,
a red line, a blue line.

00:03:34.240 --> 00:03:36.798
The general rule is that
whenever you use colors

00:03:36.798 --> 00:03:39.881
on your page, it either
has a direct meaning

00:03:39.881 --> 00:03:41.980
or the needs to be legend.

00:03:41.980 --> 00:03:44.130
And again, this will look cleaner,

00:03:44.130 --> 00:03:45.870
nicer, more sophisticated.

00:03:45.870 --> 00:03:48.130
My last comment is just switching here

00:03:48.130 --> 00:03:49.860
between these two slides.

00:03:49.860 --> 00:03:52.060
So what you see here is
that several elements

00:03:52.060 --> 00:03:53.880
are jittering, are moving.

00:03:53.880 --> 00:03:55.510
This is also something you wanna avoid.

00:03:55.510 --> 00:03:57.140
So let's look at the action type.

00:03:57.140 --> 00:03:58.410
You see, this is moving.

00:03:58.410 --> 00:04:01.710
This means that this isn't
nicely and properly aligned.

00:04:01.710 --> 00:04:02.910
And of course, this will be noticed

00:04:02.910 --> 00:04:04.650
if you save this as a PDF or whatever

00:04:04.650 --> 00:04:05.870
and you just scroll through it

00:04:05.870 --> 00:04:08.930
and you see all these elements
moving from page to page,

00:04:08.930 --> 00:04:11.800
this just looks not
aligned, not professional.

00:04:11.800 --> 00:04:13.940
The same, of course
here also with the text

00:04:13.940 --> 00:04:16.620
with these bullets and same
thing here with the footer.

00:04:16.620 --> 00:04:17.700
Why is this moving again?

00:04:17.700 --> 00:04:19.596
Make sure that you have
no jarring on your pages.

00:04:19.596 --> 00:04:22.780
This just looks unprofessional.
Next presentation.

00:04:22.780 --> 00:04:25.116
So this is apparently a
deck about Rockefeller.

00:04:25.116 --> 00:04:27.450
So some information, some facts on him.

00:04:27.450 --> 00:04:29.090
And here my first impression

00:04:29.090 --> 00:04:32.250
is that this does already
look a bit more organized,

00:04:32.250 --> 00:04:35.300
a bit more clean than the
slides that we saw before.

00:04:35.300 --> 00:04:37.900
And if you look at this,
you can see some good

00:04:37.900 --> 00:04:40.170
slide writing principles followed here.

00:04:40.170 --> 00:04:41.600
And if you're more interested in that

00:04:41.600 --> 00:04:44.210
because I cannot now go into
every little piece of that,

00:04:44.210 --> 00:04:46.840
I actually created a whole
course on slide writing,

00:04:46.840 --> 00:04:49.141
on how to create PowerPoint presentations

00:04:49.141 --> 00:04:51.730
in the style of leading consulting firms.

00:04:51.730 --> 00:04:53.387
So if you're interested with
that and wanna learn more,

00:04:53.387 --> 00:04:55.700
check out the link in
the video description.

00:04:55.700 --> 00:04:57.835
I have over 10,000
students taking the course.

00:04:57.835 --> 00:05:00.310
I trust that might be
interesting for some of you.

00:05:00.310 --> 00:05:02.650
Now, I wanna focus on this specific page

00:05:02.650 --> 00:05:04.390
and again, it looks not too bad.

00:05:04.390 --> 00:05:06.200
So it has a proper action title

00:05:06.200 --> 00:05:09.620
or the text here is of the same text size.

00:05:09.620 --> 00:05:11.420
So one thing that you
could do to further improve

00:05:11.420 --> 00:05:12.860
is add separator lines.

00:05:12.860 --> 00:05:15.840
So for some reason, this still
looks a bit unfinished to me.

00:05:15.840 --> 00:05:18.340
It seems like something is
missing here on this page.

00:05:18.340 --> 00:05:20.360
And I believe one thing
is these separator lines

00:05:20.360 --> 00:05:22.470
that you could include
between these elements

00:05:22.470 --> 00:05:23.900
to make it look a bit more organized.

00:05:23.900 --> 00:05:27.240
Then the next question is
also, so what exactly is this?

00:05:27.240 --> 00:05:29.960
So these elements are introduced here.

00:05:29.960 --> 00:05:31.500
What elements are these exactly?

00:05:31.500 --> 00:05:33.100
What am I looking at right now?

00:05:33.100 --> 00:05:35.590
What is the title, or
the organizing principle,

00:05:35.590 --> 00:05:36.670
of these elements?

00:05:36.670 --> 00:05:38.150
So if I understand this correctly

00:05:38.150 --> 00:05:40.420
also from inferring it
from the action title,

00:05:40.420 --> 00:05:42.864
this is probably something
like the competitive advantages

00:05:42.864 --> 00:05:44.610
that Rockefeller had

00:05:44.610 --> 00:05:45.830
or the things that he did,

00:05:45.830 --> 00:05:48.920
the measures that he undertook
to increase its market share.

00:05:48.920 --> 00:05:50.050
And if this is what it is,

00:05:50.050 --> 00:05:52.360
then also add this as
a little subtitle here

00:05:52.360 --> 00:05:53.750
just to make it more clean.

00:05:53.750 --> 00:05:55.843
The next one, let's look at the chart.

00:05:55.843 --> 00:06:00.120
And again, here basic slide
writing principles are followed.

00:06:00.120 --> 00:06:02.590
The one thing that I wanna
give you as general tip,

00:06:02.590 --> 00:06:04.782
and this is that whenever
you use percentages,

00:06:04.782 --> 00:06:09.460
always add the percentage
of what are you looking at.

00:06:09.460 --> 00:06:11.580
The percentage of what.

00:06:11.580 --> 00:06:14.040
One question that you could
potentially ask yourself

00:06:14.040 --> 00:06:15.100
when you look at the market share

00:06:15.100 --> 00:06:18.370
is that whether this is the
market share measured in units

00:06:18.370 --> 00:06:20.398
or the market share measured in US dollar.

00:06:20.398 --> 00:06:22.940
So this here just remains unclear

00:06:22.940 --> 00:06:24.360
and this could be easily fixed

00:06:24.360 --> 00:06:26.610
just by making your self
a habit of always writing

00:06:26.610 --> 00:06:27.790
percentage of what,

00:06:27.790 --> 00:06:30.680
solve the market units
or the market in dollars.

00:06:30.680 --> 00:06:32.500
So let's move to the next presentation.

00:06:32.500 --> 00:06:36.580
This looks like some type of
business pitch of a product

00:06:36.580 --> 00:06:40.500
which seems to be a chair that
is included in a backpack.

00:06:40.500 --> 00:06:42.510
So interesting idea for sure.

00:06:42.510 --> 00:06:44.320
Again, let's just pick
one slide to this one.

00:06:44.320 --> 00:06:45.870
Let's just focus on this.

00:06:45.870 --> 00:06:48.140
And this apparently is
the page in this document

00:06:48.140 --> 00:06:50.910
where the market and
industry for this product

00:06:50.910 --> 00:06:52.150
is supposed to be explained.

00:06:52.150 --> 00:06:53.740
So here, the first thing that you see

00:06:53.740 --> 00:06:55.840
is that it's really hard to understand

00:06:55.840 --> 00:06:58.177
what the message of all of
this really is supposed to be.

00:06:58.177 --> 00:07:01.410
What is now really the thing
that I should take away

00:07:01.410 --> 00:07:02.450
from this page?

00:07:02.450 --> 00:07:04.840
And here the clearest
thing that is missing

00:07:04.840 --> 00:07:06.080
is the action title.

00:07:06.080 --> 00:07:08.810
So here you see the title
is just market and industry.

00:07:08.810 --> 00:07:10.350
This is pretty much just the header,

00:07:10.350 --> 00:07:12.350
but a clear action title is missing

00:07:12.350 --> 00:07:14.660
and this is exactly why
it's just super difficult

00:07:14.660 --> 00:07:16.450
to really understand what the message is.

00:07:16.450 --> 00:07:18.480
If you have no idea
what I'm talking about,

00:07:18.480 --> 00:07:20.600
if you don't know what an action title is,

00:07:20.600 --> 00:07:22.691
then check out my video
that I made specifically

00:07:22.691 --> 00:07:23.800
on action titles.

00:07:23.800 --> 00:07:25.880
It's where I explain what it's all about,

00:07:25.880 --> 00:07:28.080
action title's our fundamental piece

00:07:28.080 --> 00:07:29.860
of every slide presentation.

00:07:29.860 --> 00:07:32.069
Check out the video here
to learn more about it

00:07:32.069 --> 00:07:33.440
where I discussed this in the past.

00:07:33.440 --> 00:07:34.273
And now if you look into this,

00:07:34.273 --> 00:07:36.690
you'll see again
different font sizes used.

00:07:36.690 --> 00:07:37.750
This is font 20.

00:07:37.750 --> 00:07:38.930
This is font 18.

00:07:38.930 --> 00:07:41.076
Of course this here is something
that you can barely read.

00:07:41.076 --> 00:07:42.840
The general rule is,

00:07:42.840 --> 00:07:44.720
especially for professional presentations,

00:07:44.720 --> 00:07:47.170
never just copy paste charts like that.

00:07:47.170 --> 00:07:49.230
But especially if you
already have the numbers,

00:07:49.230 --> 00:07:51.030
if they already apparently present here,

00:07:51.030 --> 00:07:53.480
just recreate the chart in PowerPoint.

00:07:53.480 --> 00:07:55.840
It will always look much
better and much cleaner.

00:07:55.840 --> 00:07:57.820
But here so much remains in the dark.

00:07:57.820 --> 00:07:59.730
So pains of the industry.

00:07:59.730 --> 00:08:02.120
What industry exactly are
you talking about here?

00:08:02.120 --> 00:08:04.760
So is this the sports and outdoor market?

00:08:04.760 --> 00:08:06.130
Is this the industry?

00:08:06.130 --> 00:08:09.030
As far as I can see, this was
also not properly introduced

00:08:09.030 --> 00:08:10.250
on the pages before.

00:08:10.250 --> 00:08:11.540
So really hard to understand.

00:08:11.540 --> 00:08:13.190
Same thing here for this chart.

00:08:13.190 --> 00:08:15.890
So what exactly is this
chart supposed to tell me?

00:08:15.890 --> 00:08:17.110
So understand that here below

00:08:17.110 --> 00:08:20.417
there's some type of market
sizing for the Portuguese market

00:08:20.417 --> 00:08:24.427
but here this chart says
user penetration worldwide.

00:08:24.427 --> 00:08:26.262
So the user penetration of what?

00:08:26.262 --> 00:08:28.100
And here as far as I understand,

00:08:28.100 --> 00:08:29.920
Portugal seems to have a rather low

00:08:29.920 --> 00:08:31.730
to medium user penetration.

00:08:31.730 --> 00:08:32.610
So what does this mean?

00:08:32.610 --> 00:08:34.102
Is this good? Is this bad?

00:08:34.102 --> 00:08:35.759
So again, I really have no idea

00:08:35.759 --> 00:08:38.650
what this page is supposed to tell me,

00:08:38.650 --> 00:08:40.287
what I'm supposed to
take out of this page.

00:08:40.287 --> 00:08:41.810
So our next presentation,

00:08:41.810 --> 00:08:43.110
this is a set of slides

00:08:43.110 --> 00:08:44.960
that apparently talk about networking.

00:08:44.960 --> 00:08:46.070
And overall, I must say,

00:08:46.070 --> 00:08:48.570
they look professional,
they look very well done.

00:08:48.570 --> 00:08:50.720
One thing though, I just
wanna put your attention

00:08:50.720 --> 00:08:52.110
is that on a page like that,

00:08:52.110 --> 00:08:54.150
there is just lots of text

00:08:54.150 --> 00:08:56.340
and in almost all situations,

00:08:56.340 --> 00:08:58.930
people will never read this much text.

00:08:58.930 --> 00:09:01.350
Even if they get this handed as a report

00:09:01.350 --> 00:09:03.430
or handed as a business presentation,

00:09:03.430 --> 00:09:05.242
this is just something
that will not be read.

00:09:05.242 --> 00:09:07.150
And what you could easily do here

00:09:07.150 --> 00:09:09.020
is just to deword the whole page.

00:09:09.020 --> 00:09:10.820
So take out lots of words

00:09:10.820 --> 00:09:13.200
by keeping the full meaning
of what you see here

00:09:13.200 --> 00:09:16.400
because indeed your
full sentences are used

00:09:16.400 --> 00:09:18.460
as if you would read a book,

00:09:18.460 --> 00:09:19.780
go on these slide presentations

00:09:19.780 --> 00:09:22.400
so you usually wanna
say as much as possible

00:09:22.400 --> 00:09:24.470
with as little words as possible

00:09:24.470 --> 00:09:26.480
just to declutter it, to deword it.

00:09:26.480 --> 00:09:28.520
And the main way to do this is of course

00:09:28.520 --> 00:09:32.750
rather use bullet points style
instead of full sentences.

00:09:32.750 --> 00:09:34.650
So just one little example,

00:09:34.650 --> 00:09:35.877
instead of writing,

00:09:35.877 --> 00:09:39.690
"The value of this information
depends on the trust

00:09:39.690 --> 00:09:40.830
within the network,"

00:09:40.830 --> 00:09:42.357
just write a bullet saying,

00:09:42.357 --> 00:09:45.310
"Information value
depends on network trust."

00:09:45.310 --> 00:09:47.270
So one little thing that you can often do

00:09:47.270 --> 00:09:50.510
to take out words is to
delete articles like "the"

00:09:50.510 --> 00:09:51.850
to deword the page.

