00:11:16.190 --> 00:11:17.980
So now to the next presentation.

00:11:17.980 --> 00:11:19.800
Here the one thing that I wanna point out

00:11:19.800 --> 00:11:22.600
is how too much graphical things,

00:11:22.600 --> 00:11:25.560
how too many animations
can really take away

00:11:25.560 --> 00:11:27.730
from the content of the slides

00:11:27.730 --> 00:11:30.510
and can even also look
unprofessional to some extent.

00:11:30.510 --> 00:11:33.420
So here, if you go over,
there are so many animations,

00:11:33.420 --> 00:11:36.790
so many colors that do not really add much

00:11:36.790 --> 00:11:39.030
to the actual content,
to the actual meaning

00:11:39.030 --> 00:11:41.460
that the things that you actually
wanna say with your slides

00:11:41.460 --> 00:11:43.180
get completely diminished.

00:11:43.180 --> 00:11:45.524
So here, just be sure that
you use graphical elements

00:11:45.524 --> 00:11:50.070
like this and bold colors like
this very, very selectively.

00:11:50.070 --> 00:11:54.190
Usually less is more and the
same is true for animations.

00:11:54.190 --> 00:11:56.578
Usually there are no animations
in presentations like this.

00:11:56.578 --> 00:11:59.300
One of the reasons being that
often these presentations

00:11:59.300 --> 00:12:00.902
are not even getting presented,

00:12:00.902 --> 00:12:03.710
but they're just printed out as documents

00:12:03.710 --> 00:12:06.230
and then you just go over
these documents in a meeting

00:12:06.230 --> 00:12:07.920
and everybody just has a handout

00:12:07.920 --> 00:12:10.810
of this presentation document
in front of him or her.

00:12:10.810 --> 00:12:13.380
But even if you are
presenting it on a display,

00:12:13.380 --> 00:12:16.240
animations is just not the look and feel

00:12:16.240 --> 00:12:18.583
that you should go for
for C level presentations.

00:12:18.583 --> 00:12:20.779
It will be perceived as unprofessional.

00:12:20.779 --> 00:12:23.550
This is just not what is expected from you

00:12:23.550 --> 00:12:24.470
in these environments.

00:12:24.470 --> 00:12:25.640
So now next one, and again,

00:12:25.640 --> 00:12:27.280
this seems to be from
a university project.

00:12:27.280 --> 00:12:28.810
And the reason why I included it

00:12:28.810 --> 00:12:30.370
is just because I wanted to show you

00:12:30.370 --> 00:12:33.944
the different type of style
that this presentation is using.

00:12:33.944 --> 00:12:35.578
This is a presentation style

00:12:35.578 --> 00:12:39.410
that you will see more
frequently in banking.

00:12:39.410 --> 00:12:40.841
So in most consulting contexts,

00:12:40.841 --> 00:12:44.770
pages like that would never
go into the main deck.

00:12:44.770 --> 00:12:46.540
It's just far too much text.

00:12:46.540 --> 00:12:49.010
Things like this would go in the back up.

00:12:49.010 --> 00:12:50.120
But for whatever reason,

00:12:50.120 --> 00:12:52.820
bankers just like to put even more words

00:12:52.820 --> 00:12:54.720
in their presentations than consultants.

00:12:54.720 --> 00:12:57.680
But this is indeed what you
will find if you join a bank.

00:12:57.680 --> 00:13:00.040
I just wanna also make you
aware of one other specialty

00:13:00.040 --> 00:13:02.197
that you often find in
these banking presentations

00:13:02.197 --> 00:13:06.100
and this is the so-called
football field chart.

00:13:06.100 --> 00:13:07.730
And this is exactly what you see here.

00:13:07.730 --> 00:13:10.850
Bankers use this all the
time to display spreads

00:13:10.850 --> 00:13:12.210
and company valuations

00:13:12.210 --> 00:13:14.070
coming from different valuation types.

00:13:14.070 --> 00:13:16.437
Well, the problem is
nobody understands this

00:13:16.437 --> 00:13:17.810
outside of banking.

00:13:17.810 --> 00:13:19.330
I tried to make charts like this

00:13:19.330 --> 00:13:21.360
several time in a consulting context

00:13:21.360 --> 00:13:25.540
and I've yet to meet a
client that can understand

00:13:25.540 --> 00:13:27.010
and read this type of chart.

00:13:27.010 --> 00:13:29.900
So my takeaway here is that
there are some differences

00:13:29.900 --> 00:13:32.360
in consulting compared
to banking presentations,

00:13:32.360 --> 00:13:34.710
though I would argue if you wanna learn

00:13:34.710 --> 00:13:37.143
the presentation style that
will make you successful

00:13:37.143 --> 00:13:39.190
in C level environments,

00:13:39.190 --> 00:13:41.781
in broad room environments
of large corporate firms,

00:13:41.781 --> 00:13:43.923
then I'd argue that the consulting style

00:13:43.923 --> 00:13:46.950
probably will be a bit
more successful for you.

00:13:46.950 --> 00:13:48.770
This is at least from my experience,

00:13:48.770 --> 00:13:50.837
what works much better
if you wanna communicate

00:13:50.837 --> 00:13:53.290
your insights to your leadership

00:13:53.290 --> 00:13:55.830
in most business situations
and environments.

